<title>BELGIUM: UM PLANS CHINA ZINC, CADMIUM OPERATIONS.</title>
<headline>UM PLANS CHINA ZINC, CADMIUM OPERATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere SA said on Wednesday it was finalising plans to produce zinc powders and cadmium oxide in China.</p>
<p>Both products are used in the manufacture of batteries.</p>
<p>&quot;The new production units are targeted to become operational in the second half of 1997,&quot; UM said in a statement.</p>
<p>UM said it could locate a production plant in Shanghai, where it already operates a cobalt powder plant.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
